1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ='''Gutthorm Guttormsson'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Guttorm Östmansson, Jarl in Jämtland and Svealand and Ingrid Guttormsdotter, at Rein
2 CONT * Brother of Helena Guttormsdatter, af Reine
2 CONT * Born eft. ca. 1180 in Svealand, Sweden. Died after 1240 in Frösö (Z) Sweden
2 CONT * Marines at Frösön.
2 CONT * Holder on Frösön. Born around 1180 in Svealand, Sweden. [B ESPELL] In the source the author describes the nobles who were mentioned in two royal letters of the year 1347; namely as herdsmen Nils in Slandrom and Olav Håkonsson in
2 CONC  Västanåker and before them is in one of the letters Guttorm Dagfinsson (grandson), who thus 'may be even more distinguished'. (Source: Jemtland and Norway, page 104, Professor Edv. Bull, 1927) (Source: Skanke family, Roger de Rob
2 CONC elin) 
2 CONT * Died after 1240 in Frösö (Z) Jämtland, Sweden
2 CONT * [https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigge_Guttormsson Sigge Guttormsson to Ljuna was a Swedish stormman from Hogstad parish near Mjölby in Östergötland, died 1283 who is considered the grandson of Earl Guttorm . He was married to B
2 CONC irger Jarls daughter Kristina Birgersdotter (died 1285).]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  '''Kristine NN''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sigge Guttormson, till Ljuna,''' birth: after  1220 in Sverige (Sweden) & death: 1283 in Östergötland, Sverige Sweden, married:  Kristina Birgersdotter (Folkungaätten)
2 CONT *  '''Erik Guttormsson,'''  Birth: circa 1240 in Frösön, Jämtland, Norge Norway & death: 1270 in Frösön, Jämtland, Norge Norway, married: 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Notes about Guttorm Guttormsson=
2 CONT
2 CONT A Gutthorm dux, mentioned 1180 (Dipl. Suec. I, nos. 59 and 66). Is this possible, which in that case brings forward the estimated time of birth by approx. 20 years both on this and probably also the children. Guttorm Jarl, (d.ä) w
2 CONC as Jarl from about 1167, to at least 1171 and thus must have resigned or died between the years 1176 - 1178, which excludes him as the mentioned Gutthorm dux 1180, unless it was a retroactive mention. (A direct quote from Dipl. Su
2 CONC ec. I, nos. 59 and 66. would be desirable to see here). Dux is also likely to be interpreted as a companion and not an Earl, as Birger Brosa was a Swedish earl between the years 1174–1202. Power holder on Frösön. Born eft. ca. 116
2 CONC 0 in Svealand, Sweden. Died after 1240 in Frösö (Z). In the source the author describes the nobles who were mentioned in two royal letters of the year 1347; namely as herdsmen Nils in Slandrom and Olav Håkonsson in Västanåker and 
2 CONC before them is in one of the letters Guttorm Dagfinsson (grandson), who thus 'may be even more distinguished'. (Source: Jemtland and Norway, page 104, Professor Edv. Bull, 1927) (Source: Skanke family, Roger de Robelin) 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
