2 CONT
2 CONT '''Guttorm & his wife had five children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''RANGRID Guttormsdotter''' married firstly BJORN Byrdasven, married secondly FREDERIK Kjona (-1164).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' RANGRID Guttormsdotter & her first husband BJORN Byrdasven had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)         '''ELRID Bjornsdotter'''  married firstly THORER Skindfeld .  m secondly MAGNUS Erlingsson King of Norway, son of ERLING Ormsen "Skakke/the Sharp" Jarl in Norway & his wife Kristin Sigurdsdotter of Norway (1156-ki
2 CONC lled in battle near Fimreite on Sognefjord 15 Jun 1184, bur Bergen, Christ's Church).
2 CONT * 2.         '''INGERID  Guttormsdotter,''' married GUTTORM Ostmansson .
2 CONT * 3.         '''GUDRUD Guttormsdotter'''
2 CONT * 4.         '''ASULF Guttormsson'''
2 CONT * 5.         '''BAARD Guttormsson of Rein''' (-1194).  Snorre names Bard as son of "Guthorm of Reine"[241].  Morkinskinna names “Guthormr at Rein” as father of “Bárdr, the father of King Ingi and Skúli jarl”[242].  m firstly ULFHI
2 CONC LD Palsdatter .  m secondly (after 15 Jun 1184) as her second husband, CECILIA Sigurdsdotter, divorced wife of FOLKVID Lagmand in Värmland, illegitimate daughter of SIGURD Haraldsson "Mund" Joint King of Norway & his mistress --- 
2 CONC (-1185).  The Saga of King Sverre records that King Sverre arranged the marriage of "his sister Cecilia" to "Bard Guthormsson of Rein"[243], dated from the context to just after the death of King Magnus [15 Jun 1184].  m thirdly R
2 CONC AGNDID Erlingsdotter . 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Baard & his second wife CECILIA Sigurdsdotter had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)         '''INGE Baardsson''' (-23 Apr 1217).  Morkinskinna names “Guthormr at Rein” as father of “Bárdr, the father of King Ingi and Skúli jarl”[244].  Snorre names "Guthorm of Reine" as grandfather of "King Inge and Duke
2 CONC  Skule", their father presumably being Baard although this is not stated in this passage[245].  King of the Birkebeiner.  He succeeded as King of Norway in 1204.  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1204 of "rex Haquinus, Sve
2 CONC rreri filius" and the succession of "Ingo Bardi filius" aged 13 [although this age appears inconsistent with the chronology of the family][246].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inge had one illegitimate child by GYRITH, daughter of ---:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>* i)          '''GUTTORM Ingesson''' (1205/6-1223/35).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Baard & his third wife RAGNDID Erlingsdotter had six children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* b)         '''SIGURD Baardsson'''
2 CONT >>>>* c)         '''ARNULF Baardsson'''
2 CONT >>>>* d)         '''GUTTORM Baardsson'''
2 CONT >>>>* e)         '''SKULI Baardsson''' (-killed in battle Oslo 1240).  Morkinskinna names “Guthormr at Rein” as father of “Bárdr, the father of King Ingi and Skúli jarl”[247].  Snorre names "Guthorm of Reine" as grandfather of "Ki
2 CONC ng Inge and Duke Skule", their father presumably being Baard although this is not stated in this passage[248].  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1217 of "rex Ingo et Philippus rex Vicensium" and the succession of "Haquini,
2 CONC  regis Haquini filii et Skulonis comitis"[249].  The Icelandic Annals record that "Haquinum regem et Schulonem comitem" divided "provinciarum Norvegiæ" in 1223[250].  "Skule jarll broder Inga konongs" and "Hakon kongr" donated pro
2 CONC perty to St Olav's church, Nidaros by charter dated 29 Sep 1225 which names "Margrettar dottor"[251].  Duke of Norway:  The Icelandic Annals record that "Rex Haqvinus" created "Skuloni…ducem" in 1238[252].  The Icelandic Annals re
2 CONC cord that "Skulo dux" gave himself "nomen regis" in 1239[253].  The Icelandic Annals record a battle between "Haquinum regem" and "Skulonem ducem" at Oslo in 1240, and that "dux Skulo et Petrus filius eius" were killed[254].  m RA
2 CONC GNHILD, daughter of ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SKULI & his wife RAGNHILD had three children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>* i)          '''MARGARETA''' (-1270).  The Icelandic Annals record the marriage in 1225 of "rex Haquinus" and "Margareta Schulonis comitis filia"[255].  "Skule jarll broder Inga konongs" and "Hakon kongr" donated property t
2 CONC o St Olav's church, Nidaros by charter dated 29 Sep 1225 which names "Margrettar dottor"[256].  m (25 May 1225) HAAKON Haakonsson King of Norway, illegitimate son of HAAKON Sverkersson King of the Birkebeiner & his mistress Inge -
2 CONC -- (posthumously 1204-Orkney [5/16] Dec 1263).
2 CONT >>>>>>* ii)         '''INGERID''' (-1232).  m (1227) KNUD Haakonsson King of the Ribbunger, son of Jarl HAAKON Galin & his wife Kristin Nilsdotter (-1261). 
2 CONT >>>>>>* iii)        '''RAGNRID''' (-after 1247).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Skuli had one illegitimate child by an unknown mistress:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>* iv)        '''PETER''' (-killed in battle Oslo 1240).  The Icelandic Annals record a battle between "Haquinum regem" and "Skulonem ducem" at Oslo in 1240, and that "dux Skulo et Petrus filius eius" were killed[257]. 
2 CONT >>>>* f)         ''' SIGRID'''.  Morkinskinna records that “Sigridr, the sister of King Ingi Bárdarson” married “Jón”, son of “Sigurdr Austrátt, a district chieftain”, who was the son of “Kári King´s brother and [his wife] Borghil
2 CONC dr the daughter of Dag Eilífsson”[258].  m firstly (1206) THORGRIM of Ljanes (-1206).  m secondly JON Sigurdsson of Osteraat, son of SIGURD Austratt & his wife --- (-1214).
2 CONT >>>>* g)        ''' INGEBORG''' m ALF von Thornberg .
