2 CONT In the 13th century, a new fiscal system was introduced and the hundreds were gradually included into larger administrative units called len, with a castle serving as the administrative center. This new administrative development 
2 CONC was a result of the increased power of the aristocracy. In each len, a noble man was put in charge, with the title lensmand.
