1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Helena Siggesdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Sigge Guttormsson, till Ljuna and Kristina Birgersdotter Folkungaätten 
2 CONT * Born: circa 1263. 
2 CONT * Death: after 1290. 
2 CONT * Received 1284-02-13 papal permission to marry Ulf Holmgersson (Ama). (See Below SDHK No: 1266)
2 CONT * Hans Gillingstam has, based on Adolf Filip Liljeholm's remark, stated that since Helena is not mentioned in Sigge Guttormsson's will, it is probable that she was Kristina Birgersdotter's daughter in an unknown previous marriage 
2 CONC 4 . Against this it can be stated that the daughter Margareta is not mentioned in Sigge's will either. Her patronymic icon is listed in the Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters in a comment about her seal being
2 CONC  Siggesdotter 5.6. For Helena, there is no preserved seal imprint, but when Margareta and Helena are mentioned together, Margareta is mentioned before Helena, which may indicate that Margareta was the older of the sisters. If the 
2 CONC information about Margareta's patronymic icon is correct, then Helena should also be the daughter of Sigge Guttormsson. The answer about the sisters' fathers should appear from a possible patronymic icon in the legend of Margareta
2 CONC 's seal imprint in Brother Emil Hildebrand, Swedish seals from the Middle Ages I: 33. - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Krok
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: (1) '''Ingemar Nielsen''' Married to the Danish knight Ingemar Nielsen who in 1278 was killed at the castle Gälakvist in Skara during the uprising against Magnus Ladulås.
2 CONT * Married (2): Pope Martin (IV) gives permission to grant an exemption for marriage between King M (agnus)'s relative Helena and '''Mr. Ulf Holmgersson (Ama),''' despite the fact that these are related in the fourth line, if it is
2 CONC  true as claimed, that peace in the kingdom between the king on the one hand side and mentioned Ulf and the other great men on the other are dependent on this marriage. They married circa 1284 February 13, of Issue: Orvieto. =Marr
2 CONC ied=  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married (1)  : Helene married firstly '''riddare Ingemar Nielsson''' (murdered in 1278, discussed in Erikskrönikan[282])
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Married (2): secondly (Papal dispensation 13 Feb 1284) her third cousin '''riddare Ulf Holmgerson till Rammshammar (who is named until 1290), their unnamed daughter marrying riddare Torkel Andersån, high counsellor of Sweden (w
2 CONC ho was named in 1311, 1318, and 1335)[283].''' The testament of Helene’s granddaughter, “Ingiburgis Thorstensdoter” [Ingeborg Torstensdotter], dated 28 Mar 1346, bequeathed property to “consanguineo meo domino Birghero Magnusson..
2 CONC .matri mee...domine Katerine Vlpsdoter...sorori mee domicelle Katerine...Laurencio Ingibyornæson...”, witnessed by “dominum Birgherum Magnusson [executor] dominam Katerinam consortem suam, dominam Elenam Thorchilsdoter, domicellam
2 CONC  Katerinam Birghersdoter, Holmgerum Thorchilssom, fratrem Johannem Allonis, dominum Thorgotum, dominum Swenungam, Jaconbum Sonæson cum uxore Hermannum Cristinam Eriksdoter, Cristinam Pætersdoter...”[284].
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Ingemar Nielsen=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Nils Krok,''' In Sigge Guttormsson's will from 1283, his wife was entrusted to distribute his weapons at his own discretion between Folkvid, Beno Byllasson, Hakvin Röde, '''Nils Krok,''' Yandus, Torkil, Peter Långe and Toke ,
2 CONC  in addition to a horse, his sword and helmet, which he gave to Yandus and his armor to be sold to finance his son Birger's tuition fee 1 . Three years before Nils Krok and his brother Ingemar sold their maternal estate in Valla, 
2 CONC a Magnus Ragvaldsson sold land in the same village 12 . It is not clear from the letter of purchase who this Magnus Ragvaldsson was, but a qualified assumption can be based on the fact that the knight Karl Bengtsson together with 
2 CONC Lars Håkansson ( beam covered with two rafters) 1344 sealed a sale in the Lekslätt adjacent to Valla in Flistads parish 14 . Karl Bengtsson's first wife was Ingrid Filipsdotter ( retrospective wolf ) who from a previous marriage h
2 CONC ad a son Magnus Ragvaldsson ( Lejonbalk ).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Ulf Holmgersson ( Ama )=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Kristina Ulfsdotter ( Ama ).''' Married to Councilor Torkel Andersson who first carried a shared shield and later a boat. Kristina was named after both her grandmothers names; Kristina Fastadotter (Plant) to Landsjö & Kristin
2 CONC a Birgersdotter Folkungaätten.  Kristina is also listed in her grandmother Kristina Fastadotter (Plant) Will, she states, And two silver flasks one another, to little Kristina a small harp will do if she lived after my own, if I d
2 CONC o not have the Lady Helena de Sco holmgeri abandoned. she donates i.a. her psaltery to little Kristina, if she survives the testator, of which Holmger's widow Helena from Sko should not have it instead.  - https://sok.riksarkivet.
2 CONC se/?Sokord=SDHK%3A+762&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_762&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab
2 CONT * '''Holmger dy Ulfsson ( Ama ).''' Appears 1304—1311 and owned estates in i.a. a. Västerrekarna hd in Södermanland. Was dead in 1323. Was married to Elena, who died no later than 1323 and was the daughter of the knight and counci
2 CONC lor Sigmund Erengislason (boat) and Birgitta Törnesdotter.
2 CONT * '''NN Ulfsdotter ( Ama ).''' Died after 1326. Married to Birger Magnusson ( Magnus Marinasson's family ) who then remarried to Katarina Olofsdotter ( Balksparre? ).
2 CONT * '''Katarina Ulfsdotter ( Ama ).''' Married first to Torsten NN and then to Ulf Magnusson ( Lejonbalk ).
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ulf+Holmgersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=13&postid=sdhk_1266&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 1266]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1284 February 13, of Issue: Orvieto'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Pope Martin (IV) gives permission to grant an exemption for marriage between King M (agnus)'s relative Helena and Mr. Ulf Holmgersson, despite the fact that these are related in the fourth line, if it is true as claimed, that peac
2 CONC e in the kingdom between the king on the one hand side and mentioned Ulf and the other great men on the other are dependent on this marriage. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/1266.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=sigge+guttormsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_1238&tab=post#tab 1238]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1283 June 11'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigge Guttormsson to Ljuna prepares his will as follows: to the monks in Alvastra, where he chooses his grave, he donates his farm in Västra Ljuna (Hogstads parish) with movable property in accordance with a previous letter (12760
2 CONC 000 b, DS 608), to the church of Näsby's estate, comprising a tooth of any new cultivation, to Salmundus, the parish priest in the church, 1 land of money, to the church in Hogstad (Hogstad parish) 1/4 eighth in "Colsthorp" to cov
2 CONC er the expenses of someone Sister Priest there, to Mr. Runstanus, Sister Priest there, 2 Mark Pence, to the Lesser Brothers in Söderköping 1 Mark Silver, to the Preacher Brothers in Skänninge 1 Mark Silver, to the Preacher Brother
2 CONC s in Skara 1 Mark Silver, to the Brothers in Skara 1 Mark Silver, to the hospital in Skara 1/2 mark silver, to the brothers in Lödöse 1 mark silver, to two hospitals in Östergötland 1 mark silver, to the monastery in Askeby 1 mark
2 CONC  silver, to the monastery of Vreta 1 mark silver, t ill brothers in Nyköping 1 mark of silver, further 1 mark of silver as a kind of replacement, which he mentioned to his father in law, and finally to the hospital at Öland 1/2 ma
2 CONC rk silver. In order to pay the above, he pledges his red clothes and 1 eighth in West Ljuna between the two farms and forbids anyone besides the monks in Alvastra or his wife to redeem this eighth. Furthermore he donates to the ch
2 CONC urch in Linköping's farm in Hogstad with all belongings and buildings1 and releases all his troops. To the prostitute Nils in Högby, he donates his black tunic with surkot and hood, to his nephew N, his lined hoodie, to his son Bi
2 CONC rger as the "schooling" the value of his own armor, since it was sold by the testament dean Dean Jng (e / mouth /?). His other weapons are to be distributed to his wife, between his friends, Beno Byllasson, Hakvin Rød, Nils Krok, 
2 CONC Yandus, Torkil, Peter Långe and Toke, in addition to a horse, his sword and helmet, which he gives to Yandus. In order to get rid of his crusade promise he dedicates two silver beads and a silver cannon, which is found at the gold
2 CONC smith Tideman in Söderköping. In addition, he pays a lot of goods to solve a number of money requirements for individuals and institutions. Witnesses are his wife Kristina, the linking schnapps Svennung and Birger, magician Otto, 
2 CONC brother Knut from Söderköping and his priest Nils, who also sealed together with the issuer and the linköping chapter. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000025565454677&photo_id=6000000138090200144&p
2 CONC osition=0
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=sigge+guttormsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=2&postid=sdhk_1286&tab=post#tab 1286]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1285 without day'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Kristina, Birger Earl's daughter (and widow of Mr. Sigge Guttormsson to Ljuna), establishes his testament as follows: To the monks of Alvastra, with whom she chose her graveyard with her husband, she donates the farm Ljuna (Hogsta
2 CONC ds socken, Göstrings (1 in its entirety with the exception of an oath and a plot, which with all its belongings is inevitably linked to its farm "walled"; this is, however, subject to all returns of the farm (Ljuna?) annually on 2
2 CONC 9/8 shall be paid in return for the whole convention, if possible in the form of a joint extradition, and celebrating her anniversary. Furthermore, she donates to Linköping's cathedral, the Normlösa farm, where on the bishop's beh
2 CONC alf an altar will be established Week two fairs will be held for the dead, one for the Virgin Mary and a death fair for her deceased husband (2. Finally, she also donates 1 mark of silver to each monastery In Sweden, with the exce
2 CONC ption of those in Gotland and Finland, for night quarters and 1/2 mark silver for each hospital in the Kingdom. Sigillants are the issuer, King M (agnus), his brother Duke B (eng) of Finland, Bishop B. (wrong for H.?) In Linköping
2 CONC  and the daughters of the issue Margaret and Helena. Witnesses were Abbot Nils in Alvastra and Kristina's confessor brother Knut from Söderköping. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000009365755840&ph
2 CONC oto_id=6000000143167703111&position=0
2 CONT
