1 NAME Margareta /Siggesdotter/
2 GIVN Margareta
2 _MARNM Siggesdotter
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 1270
2 PLAC Som medbeseglare av ett testamente 1285, ser det idiotiskt ut med ett blankt fält som Geni genererar till en uppskattning av att ha kunnat varit född efter 1285.
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1305
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Margareta Siggesdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Sigge Guttormsson, till Ljuna and Kristina Birgersdotter (Bjälboätten) 
2 CONT * Kristina Birgersdotter's will from 1285 is preserved. As a sealer of the mother's will, there are two daughters from an early marriage - Margareta and Helena Kristinadotter who should most likely have been adults at this time. (
2 CONC Source: Bo Theutenberg - Folk kings and crusaders)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=20&Sokord=Kristina&EndastDigitaliserat=False&FacettLimits=IfjiTQ%3A0&AvanceradSok=True&page=14&postid=sdhk_1204&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab
2 CONC  '''1204''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1282 April 1'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta, Mrs. Kristina's daughter , announces that she is handing over the estate she exchanged with the Provost Peter in Ramsta in his care, free from all attack and blame.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000004378542470&photo_id=6000000178117737017&position=0 '''The issuer seals. SEAL: The seal fell off from the strip cut from the letter.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT =Näsby in Åkerbo hd, Östergötland=
2 CONT
2 CONT Letter number: 1286 Date of issue: 12850000 b Place of issue: Date comment: Language: Latin DS number: DS 800 SD number: Issuer: Kristina, Birger jarls dotter. Contents: Kristina, Birger Jarl's daughter (and widow of Mr. Sigge Gut
2 CONC tormsson to Ljuna), draws up her will as follows: To the monks in Alvastra, with whom she and her husband chose their burial place, she donates the farm Ljuna (Hogstads parish, Göstrings härad) (1 in its entirety with the exceptio
2 CONC n of an eight and a plot, which she with all additions inextricably links to her farm "wallær"; this is done, however, on condition that all returns of the said farm (Ljuna?) annually on 29/8 She will donate the farm Normlösa (Nor
2 CONC mlösa parish) to Linköping Cathedral, where an altar will be erected on behalf of the bishop, at which each week two masses will be held for the dead, one for the Virgin Mary and a death mass for her deceased husband (2. Finally, 
2 CONC she also donates 1 mark of silver to every monastery in Sweden, with the exception of those on Gotland and in Finland, for communion wine and 1/2 mark silver for every hospital in the country. Sealants are the issuer, King M (agnu
2 CONC s), his brother Duke B (engt) of Finland, Bishop B. (wrong for H.?) In Linköping and the issuer's daughters Margareta and Helena. The witnesses were Abbot Nils in Alvastra and Kristina's confessor brother Knut from Söderköping.
2 CONT
2 CONT Letter number: 928 Date of issue: 12730205 Place of issue: Bjälbo Date comment: Language: Latin DS number: DS 566 SD number: Issuer: Duke Erik, son of the late earl / Duke B. Contents: (Duke) Erik, son of the late earl / Duke B., 
2 CONC announces that in the presence of sensible and credible men he has awarded his sister Kristina two eights in Näsby and a half eighth in "Vengj".
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Kristina Birgersdotter's will from 1285 is preserved. As a sealer of the mother's will, there are two daughters from an early marriage - Margareta and Helena Kristinadotter. (Source: Bo Theutenberg - Folk kings and crusaders) So
2 CONC urces 1) Bo Theutenberg - Folk kings and crusaders, Born 1245. [1] 
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcripts:  Brocman: Misc. 1:28
2 CONT * The letter is attached to a parchment strip with fragments of Latin text. See O. Ferm in Kyrka och socken (1991), p. 380 n. 5. Ang. Ramsta parish, see DMS 1: 6, p. 128.
