1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Mette Eriksdatter Rotfeld=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Mette Eriksdatter datter av Erik Nielsen Rotfeld til Bratskov og Ellen Axelsdatter Dotting 
2 CONT * Hun var gift med Morten Nielsen Vognesen Niels Pallesen og''' Inngjerd Jepsdatter.''' ??? OBS!!  OBS!
2 CONT
2 CONT De hadde barna  Ida, Ingerd, Vogn, Niels og Johan
2 CONT
2 CONT Februar 1508 Mageskifte Aalborg Helligaandshus, og væbner Vogn Mortensen, der fik en gaard i Gærum mod en gaard i Hyllested, Suldrup. Vogn Mortensen var af slægten Vognsen af Stenshede, søn af Morten Nielsen og Mette Eriksdatter R
2 CONC otfeld og var gift med Kirsten Lauridsdatter Viffert, datter af Laurids Viffertsen (Viffert) til Rebstrup og Gyde Lauridsdatter Krag.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Kilder==
2 CONT
2 CONT # Thiset, Hiort-Lorenzen, Bobé, Teisen. Danmarks Adels Aarbog. Dansk Adelsforening, DAA 1912:429, 5.
2 CONT # https://finnholbek.dk/getperson.php?personID=I18822&tree=2
2 CONT # http://www.roskildehistorie.dk/stamtavler/adel/Kierulf/Rotfeld.htm
2 CONT # http://www.protokoller.dk/diplomatariumhornumnse/Diplomatarium%20Hornumense%20del%201.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Morten Nielsen Vognsen of Stone Heath d. Aft 1475 mentioned no earlier than 1440 (so), 1445 to Vitth. Anders Peetz, 1448 in Rolsø, medbeseglede Knud Delete, 1450 (in Rolsø) for Canute Delete (Seal: S MORTEN: Neilsen), p. A. Donald
2 CONC  Peetz, was in 1454 among the nobles, who were accused of having robbed goods from Substitute in Aarhus, 1459 Medvidne in against the ruling against Thord Thomessen in Dalsgaard (seal), 1462 (of Ellingsgaard) sold together with th
2 CONC e sons Niels and Johan Mortensen Niels Eriksen (Rotfeld) of Bratskov all that part of Bratskov, there was fallen to them by Erik Nielsen (Rotfeld) (her father) to the Bratskov (seal), 1465 of Ellingsgaard, 1466 with the Son Niels 
2 CONC Mortensen and Nis Vognsen Medvidne on Elling Kirkegaard, 1467 in Ellingsgaard, 1470 even in E, conveyed in 1472 (of Lengsholm ) a farm in Snæbum to Mariager Abbey; 1475 (of Lengsholm) to Vitth. Henrik Kalf.  Father Erik Nielsen Ro
2 CONC tfeld, to Bratskov and Holmegaard, d. 1452, Bratskov Gods, Brovst (Baltic He H., Hjørring)  Mother Ellen Axelsdatter Dotting 
2 CONT
2 CONT Viet Morten Nielsen Vognsen of Stone Heath d. Eft. 1475  Children  1. carriage Mortensen Vognsen of stone Heath, d.. 1513	  2. Ingerd Mortensdatter Vognsen of stone Heath, d.. 1465	  3. Niels Mortensen Vognsen of stone Heath, d.. 
2 CONC 1468	  4. Johan Mortensen Vognsen of stone hot, to Hjerm BramslevGaard, d.. 1463	 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mette Eriksdatter Rotfeld, to Bratskov  February 1508 Mage Switching Aalborg Helligaandshus and squire wagon Mortensen, who received a farm in Gærum on a farm in Hyllested, Suldrup. Carriage Mortensen was of the genus Vognsen of S
2 CONC tone Heath, son of Morten Nielsen and Mette Eriksdatter Rotfeld and was married to Kirsten Lauridsdatter Viffert, daughter of Laurids Viffertsen (Viffert) to Rebstrup and Gyde Lauridsdatter Krag.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rotfeld - crest (coat of arms)  race Rotfelds weapons: In red field three silver-Ibskaller (2.1), on the helmet two Goosenecks holding a golden-ring with a blue stone. 
