1 NAME Anne /Ogard/
2 GIVN Anne
2 SURN Ogard
2 _MARNM Crane
2 NICK Anne Arundell
2 NICK Anne Agard
2 NICK Anne Ogard
2 NICK Anne Hogard
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC St Mary
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 Chilton
3 CTRY England
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1442
2 PLAC Brandenham, Norfolk, England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 15 MAY 1521
2 PLAC Chilton, Suffolk, England
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A photo of her tomb can be found here
2 CONT https://amymcelroy.substack.com/p/st-marys-chilton-and-the-cranes
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Ogard/Hogard names her parents as Andrew & Alice in her will. Her will appears to be dated 6th September 1508 in the 20th year of the reign of Henry 7th. However, that date was in fact in the 24th year of Henry 7th reign, so 
2 CONC this is likely a clerical error & that the will probably dates to 6th September 1504. The heir of her husband Robert Crane fits better with this date too. See http://www.oxford-shakespeare.com/Probate/PROB_11-16-283.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT However, the will was not proved until the 15th May 1521, so it is not clear when Anne actually died.
2 CONT
2 CONT In her will she leaves money to pray for the following; herself, her parents Andrew & Alice, her grandmother Alice, her two husbands Remfrey Arundell & Robert Crane, her children; Ralph Arundell, Anne Crocker, Sir Edmund Arundell,
2 CONC  Remfrey Arundell, George Crane.
