1 NOTE We have no knowledge of the year of his birth or death, nor do we 
2 CONT know the name of his spouse. In 1448 he was residing at the 
2 CONT "fogdegård" (farm of the rural tax collector) in Vadum, Sogn, and was 
2 CONT the tax collector in Kjær township. He is also mentioned in 1450 and 
2 CONT 1454. He had apparently died before 1458, for at that time Thord 
2 CONT Nilsen was the tax collector in Kjær township. Thus it appears that 
2 CONT when he died none of his sons was of legal age, since the office of 
2 CONT tax collector in Kjær was connected to the Kjærulf family from 
2 CONT medieval times up to the end of the 17th century.
2 CONT Dyreskjøt contends that Anders Andersen Kjærulf #1 had a daughter who 
2 CONT was married at Vested in Aaby parish. Her name is not known. This 
2 CONT daughter had a son, Klement Andersen, who was born in 1484 and called 
2 CONT Skipper Klement. He was executed in 1536. Dyreskjøt writes that he " 
2 CONT betrayed both himself and the Kjærulf family as a result of his 
2 CONT failures in wartime".
2 CONT Anders Andersen Kjærulf's sons were Peder Andersen Kjærulf, Jens 
2 CONT Andersen Kjærulf and Anders Andersen Kjærulf. We shall follow the 
2 CONT line of the youngest.
1 NOTE 1485 - 1494 Aslund og Fogedgård i Øster Halne Vadum sogn
2 CONT Nævnes af Dyrskjøt 1470: "Hand eigede Aslund, Fogetgaard och megit gods".
2 CONT Var Herredsfoged i Kjær herred 1485 og 1494
1 NOTE Ejer af Aslund Fogedgaard og meget gods 14... Nævnes som foged for Kjær Herred i 1485.
