1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Kristina Ulfsdotter (Ama)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Ulf Holmgersson (Ama) and Helena Siggesdotter 
2 CONT * Kristina was named after both her grandmothers names; Kristina Fastadotter (Plant) to Landsjö  & Kristina Birgersdotter Folkungaätten
2 CONT * Kristina is listed in her grandmother Kristina Fastadotter (Plant) Will, she states, And two silver flasks one another, to little Kristina a small harp will do if she lived after my own, if I do not have the Lady Helena de Sco h
2 CONC olmgeri abandoned. she donates i.a. her psaltery to little Kristina, if she survives the testator, of which Holmger's widow Helena from Sko should not have it instead - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=SDHK%3A+762&EndastDigitali
2 CONC serat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_762&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab
2 CONT * Was married to the knight and councilor Torkel Andersson (shared shield, later boat), who calls Holmger Ulfsson dy his "genes" 1311, seals brother Lars Ulfsson's first will in 1318 and Ulf Holmgersson d. Y's will in 1335 and pro
2 CONC bably had a son named Holmger, named after one of his early deceased uncles. - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ama#TAB_2
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives  of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT == '''SDHK No:'''[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Torkel+Andersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_2405&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 2405]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1311 March 12, of Issue: Stockholm'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Torkel Andersson announces that he and his brother-in-law Holmger Ulfsson (dy) exchanged property in such a way that he hands over to him and his heirs 2 farms in Torpa, 2 farms in Mellby (Mälby in Torshälla parish) and 2 mills in
2 CONC  Torshälla while Holmger gave the issuer and his heirs their estates in Länna (?; "Lennom") and Kalvstad. Witnesses and sailors are Mr. Mattias Kettilmundsson, Mr. Sigmund Erengislesson, Mr. Torkel Djäkne, Lars Ulfsson and Nils Vä
2 CONC nundsson. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/2405.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == '''SDHK No:''' [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Torkel+Andersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=122&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C&postid=sdhk_4146&tab=post#tab 4146]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1335 April 5
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulf Holmgersson, canoe in Uppsala and Västerås, wills to Uppsala Cathedral's building, where he chooses to be buried, a farm in Helgestad, and to improve the prebend he held in Västerås 6 Öresland in Ulsa and 1 Öresland in Vikby. 
2 CONC He decides numerous gifts in the form of money and other things to. a. Strängnäs Cathedral, Linköping Cathedral, Vårfruberga Monastery, [https://www.geni.com/people/Kristina-Holmgersdotter-Ama/6000000009702795258?through=600000000
2 CONC 6820469588 Kristina Holmgersdotter] Alvastra Monastery, Nydala Monastery, Varnhem Monastery, Julita Monastery, Preachers Brothers in Strängnäs, Sigtuna, Västerås, Skara, Lödöse, Frännaö, Skänninge, Kalänninge Söderköping, Linköpin
2 CONC g, Jönköping, Skara, Arboga, Enköping, on to Sko monastery, Askeby monastery, S: take Klara monastery in Stockholm, the whole house in Uppsala, the leprosy house in Enköping, the hospital in Strängnäs, Söderköping, Skänninge,
2 CONT
2 CONT King Magnus, Torkel Andersson, Birger Magnusson, and the issuer seal, SEAL
2 CONT The seal: N: o 1-5 away, the strips left; N: o 6, Ulf Holmgerssons (3 plugs). - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000049027095883&photo_id=6000000140042367915&position=0
2 CONT
