1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sigge Birgersson Gumsehuvud=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Birger Siggesson (gumsehuvud)
2 CONT * Gallowglass Siggy Birger's son, who was named in the documents 1405 – 1417 and in the weapon brought a bagghuvud, and apparently owned Forstena (he was 1413 residing in Väne hundred).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ingrid Siggesdotter (gumsehuvud),''' Esger Torbjörnssons appear during the years 1415–1435, the latter married 1418 at Forstena with Ingrid Siggesdotter, daughter of the gunman Sigge Birgersson, who is mentioned in the docume
2 CONC nts 1405–141
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Urgammal salvation, introduced in 1625.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The eater, which originated from the aboriginal eagles (see the plain eagles Bagge of Berga). received the name "Forstenasläkten" after its former main building, Forstena, in Tunhems socken, in Vänehärd Älvsborg County, which was 
2 CONC first acquired quite late. This farm was previously occupied by a man who initially brought a naval leaf, which later became a backbone. Of this older Forstena-ayr the following known. The brothers Åke and Esger Torbjörnssöner per
2 CONC form during the years 1415-1435, the later poison 1418 at Forstena with Ingrid Siggesdotter, daughter of the warden Sigge Birgersson, who is mentioned in the documents 1405-1417, and in the arms brought a rear head, and apparently
2 CONC  owned Forstena (he was 1413 resident of Väne härad). Both of these brothers brought an untouched sea leaf or heart to the weapon. The chieftain in Vänehärd Torbjörn Esgersson, apparently son of Esger, took up the grandfather's we
2 CONC apon, the head of the head, which he brought in 1459 and later, as well as his son Gudmund Torbjörnsson, ruler of the fathers of 1486-1495, whose daughter, Forstena, went to the younger Forstena family. If there were any relatives
2 CONC  between them and Sven Brynjulfsson, who brought the back of the head, is not known. The eater has branched out into the nasty eagles Torstenson, No. 7. Another branch of the eater has been introduced especially with the name Ultf
2 CONC ana.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Sigge+Birgersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Sigge+Birgersson&AvanceradSok=True&page=7&postid=sdhk_16480&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 16480]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating:1405 April 24,of issue Tornnevalla church''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigge Birgersson, hh in Åkerbo hd , issues a fixed letter regarding a shift in which Karl in Tamäng to Jösse Mickelsson resigned land in Herrbeta and "Gåselöth" in exchange for land in Grimstad in (Östra) Skrukeby sn.
2 CONT
2 CONT All of these letters hear or see the health of Sigge Bergeson with our Lord, the Hereditary Chief of Åkerbohered. Kennes iagh with minus attendant öpno breffni might have attached to the lazy reason to man Carl in Tamängh about th
2 CONC e land he swapped with Josze Michelson, 3 span and 1 fierdingz span deposited in Herbeto and in Gåselott 5 buckle affgeldh for 15 buckle affgeldh in Grimstaden in Skruke ; Josze exaggerated - - - - gaff prescribed Carl to 3 lands 
2 CONC between the land he was dealing with, in wto and torro, inward and outward, were not exempt, of your age of age allowed. Thette breff is giord with witnom and stadh attached to right tingzstadh and right tingzdagh; thesse woro å f
2 CONC asten: Daan in Skagestaden, Steenar samestadz, Joen in Obbatorpet, Rawalder in Greenby, Ericker sammestädz, Gudmunder in Talgestaden, Nils in Skackelstaden, Lars in Vlelfue, Benchter congregation, Gunner in Ulelfue, Gisle in Herbe
2 CONC te, Suno samestadh This pre-requisite land was legal upbudin and legal standing. To me more wisso and witnesbördh also hang my seal for this letter. Date in ecclesia Törnewalla, anno Domini 1405. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokum
2 CONC ent/sdhk/16480.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Birger+Siggesson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Birger+Siggesson&AvanceradSok=True&page=1&postid=sdhk_6493&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 6493]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Prebendary of Linköping Birger Siggesson draws up his will dating, December 1352=
2 CONT
2 CONT The prebendary of Linköping Birger Siggesson draws up his will. He donates 60 land money to the cathedral in Linköping building, which Ulf Håkansson owes him; to the Archdeacon Magnus ten marvels, etc., to Leco two silver cups and
2 CONC  his better silver belt, to the sacristan Nils a silver cup, to Nils Jonsson a psalterium. Further gifts to Jonarus Esgeri, Conradus, Askeby and Vreta monastery, Nils in Stång, Johannes Puke and others.
2 CONT
2 CONT n the name of the Lord, Amen. In the Incarnation M ° ccclii on St. Lucia will Byrgerus Siggonis, prebendarius church Lyncopensis, be a severe illness, was still healthy and unharmed, and the goods to which God will write and will 
2 CONC in this manner. In the early construction of the church Lyn [c] opensis said read marks sixty pence, in which the owner Vlpho Hakunsson to do so, as in his letters about this fully contained. Also the Great archidyachono ten mardi
2 CONC linas off with one of Renault and its Sela. (1) Chief Marcho breuiarie will be better and a cup of silver. The lemons two cups of silver and silver belt is better. Ingeualdo the belt, one silver, one mortar and one of furs and ski
2 CONC ns mardilinis sleeves. Sir Nicholas Sacristan a cup of silver. Sir Nicholas Ionsson a lute. The ionarius Esgerus one pair of clothes with its furraturis. Conrad played with the silver cup with one hand and a lantern. Also any cora
2 CONC li an elder half marcham money. Campanario place only. Church of St. Lawrence place Blodsverging cured only. Campanario place the two coasts. Brothers serving III March pence piece of skin from his brother Ingemari Vrsini. Holy Sp
2 CONC irit marks the fourth house money. Church Thyrnauallum III March. I March Askaby confinement. I March vretu confinement. Also Nicholas of Stang, my dear cousin, one bowl and the silver two hooves of vulture wings, while those suma
2 CONC rios his chair and one thakhut. Stephen Stangaberg a better horn, which have wings and a belt. In the lonari Nesbyt single chair covered with a cloth. Lord Charles ...... ST. dhumos a silver spoon. Sir John Puka a spoon and a mett
2 CONC o with one of the mortar. Also Steward and my daughter four weights of red cloth, also half a piece of the heart [i] rights, X March pence a bed with all Preparamento, one red, one pot, one pot for Humulo and a basin, also sorcoci
2 CONC um is bright red, with furraturis the hood. Also servants about my daily fourteen weights white popirst. Also each of the horse, the sword and the cap iron clippeo. Items were older, single pot. Also östan servant when I had my bo
2 CONC ots and spurs. Also Harald Scrømpt a sword with a steel cap. Also, my maid Gyertrudi my white tunic. Also Sigrid my niece a front axle and a culcedram. Also linked to Margaret Neighbor mine, one cow. Then Nicholas pellipario wear 
2 CONC my blauio. Items Bagga Sudurcopie my shoes mixed color with a hood. Also Peter Vglo skin vaccines. Exequtores of this sort of testament I make honorable and that the men of the masters of the Marchis, Leçon the canons, if Ingeuald
2 CONC um prebendary and Nicholas de Stang above-mentioned stages, of which the seals together with the seal of my present need to communiri, feet, and besought, and binding it with the said exequtores, so that through me, and it was ord
2 CONC ained effectively more perfect: such and which are less properly and to do in comparison with Suppleant as they should answer before God. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000011875555759&photo_id=60
2 CONC 00000133404107056&position=0
