1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Grev Niels af Nørre Halland ejer godset Egholm i Sæby Sogn vest for Roskilde, han er søn af Niels Valdemarsen, frillesøn af Valdemar Sejr af danmark, Valdemar sejers  anden frillesøn Knud blev Hertug i reval og ægt
2 CONC ede en fyrstedatter, Knud blev stamfader til Skarholm slægten
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sorce:  (AFN: FHS3-6D)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/DENMARK.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT King Valdemar I had one illegitimate child by Mistress (1):
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.              NIELS Valdemarsen (-[1218/19]).  The Annales Ryenses name "Nicolao filio illegitimo [Waldemari Regis]" specifying that his father granted him "comitatum Hallandiæ"[508].  Count of Halland 1218.  m (1217) ODA von Sc
2 CONC hwerin, daughter of GÜNZEL II Graf von Schwerin & his wife Oda --- (-[1218/19]).  Heiress of ½ Schwerin.
2 CONT
2 CONT a)              NIELS ([1218]-1251, bur Sorø).  Count of Halland.  The Annales Ryenses record the death in 1251 of "comes Nicolaus"[509].  m as her first husband, CECILIE Jensdatter [Galen], daughter of JENS Jakobsen [Galen] & his
2 CONC  wife Adelheid Gräfin von Dassel.  She married secondly (1252) R. Anders Olufsen [Glug] (-1270).
2 CONT
2 CONT i)               NIELS (-1271).
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)              ANDERS.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii)            JAKOB (-1308).  The Annales Lubicenses record that "Iacobus" obtained the "cometiam Hallandiæ" in 1283[510].  Count of Halland.
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)            NIELS III (-murdered 1314).  Count of Halland.
2 CONT
2 CONT (b)            VALDEMAR (-murdered 1314).  Count of Halland.
2 CONT
2 CONT (c)            EUPHEMIA .  m HENNING I von Putbus (-1351/2).
2 CONT
2 CONT iv)             CÆCILIA .  m TYGE Thorstensen.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
