1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Remfrey Arundell was the elder of two sons born to Sir Remfrey Arundell and Joan Colshull. He was found to be aged 9 when his father died in 1444, so born in 1435. He married Anne Hogard and had a daughter Anne & a
2 CONC  son Edmund. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/52ee3245-bf2f-4f21-be25-b48c37f4c11d
2 CONT Reference:	AR/2/122 Court Roll
2 CONT 1444, 17th Sep [23 Hen VI]; court = c11
2 CONT c6. Death of Remfrey Arundell, knight, who held by knight's service in Wyndesor; relief; his son is under age, being aged 9, so land is seised into lord's hands. Death of Thomas Knapp, who held at Trewarueneth.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://soc.genealogy.medieval.narkive.com/Cd5drh3K/hiwis-blanchminster-turet-etc
2 CONT IPM of Joan Houghton 13 Henry VII
2 CONT Inquisition taken at Launceston 12 March [1497/8] before Peter
2 CONT Eggecombe, knt., and Roger Holaund esq., ~feodaries of the duchy of
2 CONT Cornwall, by the oath of etc; who say that in trinity term 1 Hen.VII
2 CONT [1486] a fine was levied between Robert Throgmerton and Edward Bartlet,
2 CONT plaintiffs, and William Houghton kt., and Joan his wife deforciants of
2 CONT the manors of Byenamye [Binhamy], Stratton, Swancote, St Mary Wke, St.
2 CONT Cler Colshill, Leskerdcolshill and Wykenurg with lands [details given]
2 CONT and 20s. rent there and in Tremyeth and the advowson of St. Mary Wyke
2 CONT which were by that fine settled on the said William and Joan and her
2 CONT heirs with remainders to Thomas Nevell kinsman and heirs of William
2 CONT Nevell of Pykell, chr. and. the right heirs of Guy de Blanchminster late
2 CONT rector of Lansalos.
2 CONT Joan died. 20 Dec. 13 Hen.VII. [1497]; William is yet living and holds
2 CONT the lands, the reversion whereof belongs to Edmund Arundel kt, kinsman
2 CONT of said. Joan, son of Renfrew her son and heir.
2 CONT The manor of Byenamye is held of the prince of Launceston Castle in the
2 CONT duchy by knights service, worth by the year, clear, £10.
2 CONT The manor of Stratton held. in like manner worth &c., £20.
2 CONT The manor of Swanicotte ditto; worth &c., 40s.
2 CONT The manor of St. Mary Wyke ditto; worth with the bororough and advowson
2 CONT by the year clear £10.
2 CONT The manor of St. Cler Colshill held of Richard Dyrlyng by feailty worth
2 CONT &c., £6.
