1 NAME Anne /Arundell/
2 GIVN Anne
2 SURN Arundell
2 _MARNM Crocker
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1463
2 PLAC Norfolk
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 AUG 1507
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anne9 Arundell, died 1507. She married John Croker. Her death sine prole (without issue) served as the legal catalyst for the Great Partition, as the direct Arundell-Colshull line failed.[^17]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Arundell was the only daughter of Remfrey Arundell and his wife Ann Ogard. She, along with her siblings were listed in her mother's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Anne Crane,  proved 15 May 1521, TNA PROB 11/20/165, which contains these clauses
2 CONT Item, I will that one Mass be sung at Scala Celi in Rome for the souls of me, Dame Anne
2 CONT Arundell; Andrew and Alice, my father and mother; Dame Alice, my grandam; Sir Ralph [sic Remfrey]
2 CONT Arundell, knight, Robert Crane, esquire, sometime my husbands; Ralph Arundel, Anne
2 CONT Crocker, Sir Edmund Arundell, knight, Raynfrey Arundell, George Crane, my children;
2 CONT Sir William. Lord Lovell; Dame Alice, his wife; Sir Ralph, Lord Sudley; Alice Ogard, my
2 CONT niece, and I will that the priest have their surnames written. . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne married John Crocker but had no issue. When she died in 1507, her IPM identified her heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan Colshull had two daughters named Elizabeth by her husband Renfrey Arundell of Treloy & Trefink as well as a son Renfrey d 1468 and John, Bishop of Exeter. The first Elizabeth married Sir Edward Stradling and William Lygon, th
2 CONC e second William Whittington and Nicholas Brome. Joan Colshull's heir was her granddaughter Anne (Arundell) Croker. When Anne died s.p. in 1507 her heirs were found to be: the granddaughter of the first Elizabeth Arundell, Anne St
2 CONC radling, the son of the second Elizabeth Arundell, John Whittington and the son of Joan Colshull's daughter by her second marriage to John Nanfan, Richard Bolles. The inheritance was substantial as Joan Colshull had been an heires
2 CONC s and her husband Renfrey Arundell had significant landholdings which had also descended to Anne (Arundell) Croker.
2 CONT
2 CONT 366. ANNE CROCKER.
2 CONT
2 CONT Writ 30 October, inquisition 20 May, 23 Henry VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT The said Anne and John Crokker, late her husband, were seised in fee of the under-
2 CONT mentioned manors, fourth part, messuages and lands &c., (fn. 3) and in Michaelmas
2 CONT term, 20 Henry VII, suffered a recovery thereof to Richard, bishop of Winchester,
2 CONT Giles Daubeny, knight, lord Daubeny, Thomas Lovell, knight, Thomas Marrowe, Lewis
2 CONT Pollarde, serjeant-at-law, James Hobarde, knight, Edmund Dudley, Thomas Lucas, John
2 CONT Gylberd, John Willemer and Andrew Ogarde, to the use and intent that the recoverors
2 CONT should by deed indented demise the same to the said John and Anne, or persons to be
2 CONT named by them, for 8 years from Michaelmas, 20 Henry VII, without impeachment of
2 CONT waste, at yearly rents of . . l. 6s. 8d. for the first 7 years and 38l. 6s. 8d. for
2 CONT the last year to be paid to the recoverors to the use of the king, his heirs and
2 CONT assigns, in satisfaction of 255l. and of 250l., as appears in certain indentures dated
2 CONT 16 November, 20 Henry VII, made between the said bishop of Winchester, Giles Daubeny,
2 CONT Thomas Lovell, J[ames] Hobard, Richard Empson, knights, Edmund Dudley, Thomas Marowe,
2 CONT [Lewis] Pollarde, Thomas Lucas, John Gylberd, John Willemer and Andrew [Ogarde], of
2 CONT the one part, and John Crokker and Anne his wife, sister and heir of Edmund Arundell,
2 CONT knight, of the other part. A clause in the said indenture stipulated that if the said
2 CONT John and Anne, their heirs, executors or assigns, should make default of the said
2 CONT yearly rent of 3l. 6s. 8d. payable during the first 7 years of the said term, or of
2 CONT the rent of 38l. 6s. 8d. payable for the last year, or should fail to satisfy the king
2 CONT of the said 250l. out of the issues and profits of the manor of Tremethert (whereof
2 CONT lady Joan Arundell, widow of Edmund Arundell, knight, is now seised for life), then it
2 CONT should be lawful for the recoverors to re-enter the premises and hold them to the use
2 CONT of the king, his heirs or executors, until they should have paid what remained unpaid
2 CONT of the said sums of 255l. and 250l. After payment of the said sums, the recoverors
2 CONT will stand seised of the premises to the use of the said John Crokker and Anne and the
2 CONT heirs and assigns of Anne, and will make a lawful estate thereof to them or to persons
2 CONT to be named by them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne, wife of John Danvers, knight, and John Whytyngton, esquire, are the next heirs
2 CONT of the said Anne Crocker; Anne Danvers being the daughter of John Stradlyng son of
2 CONT Elizabeth the elder sister of Remfrey Arundell, father of the said Anne Crokker, and
2 CONT John Whytyngton being the son of Elizabeth the younger sister of the said Remfrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORNWALL. Manor of Trenant, worth 10 marks, held of Robert Aysthorp, clerk,
2 CONT service unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manors of Maneley and Seint Ewea with the advowson [of the church] of the manor of
2 CONT Seint Ewea, worth 12l., held of the king in chief by service of one knight’s fee and
2 CONT by the service of finding a man riding armed in the king’s war for forty days at his
2 CONT own cost.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fourth part of the manor of Trurubourgh, worth 10s., held of the prince in free
2 CONT burgage, by fealty only.
2 CONT
2 CONT The castle or island of Sully, held of the prince, as of the castle of Launceston, by
2 CONT the service called ‘Wayternefe’ and a rent of 300 puffin or 6s. 8d. yearly; worth
2 CONT 100s. in time of peace, and in time of war nothing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Eglyshell, worth 40s., held of the bishop of Exeter, as of the manor of
2 CONT Burnier, by fealty and 9s. 9d. rent yearly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Trevenell, worth 6l., held of the aforesaid bishop, as of his manor of
2 CONT Tregeyere, service unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Truruvyan, worth 10s., held of the lord prince, as of his manor of Moreske,
2 CONT parcel of his duchy of Cornwall, by fealty and a rent of 81s. 2d. yearly, and by
2 CONT common suit to the court of Moreske.
2 CONT
2 CONT 200 messuages, 1000a. land, 100a. meadow, 1000a. pasture, [200a.] wood, [1000a.
2 CONT furze], 1000a. heath and 100s. rent in Manely, Seynt Ewa, Trenant, Sully, Lamborne,
2 CONT Trevenell, Eglyshell, Boskenna, Trebugrel, Treruvyan, Trurubourgh, Kelestoke,
2 CONT Melenowith, Mousehoule, Talgraken, Gudderon, Tresula, Redruyth, Walle, Mawle,
2 CONT Boskennan, Trevrythall and Nansmura; whereof the lands &c. in Lambourne, Kelestoke,
2 CONT Melynoweth, … . ., Talgraken and Goodron, worth 40s., are held of Richard Boscallen,
2 CONT service unknown, and the lands &c. in Tresula, Redruyth, Walle, Mawle, Boskennam,
2 CONT Trevrythall and Nansmura, worth 10l., are held of the prince, as of his manor of
2 CONT Tywarnayle, parcel of the duchy of Cornwall, for a rent of 8s. 11d. and common suit to
2 CONT the court of the said manor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne late the wife of Remfrey Arundell, knight, held for life at the time of the death
2 CONT of Anne Crocker, and still holds, the under-mentioned manors and fourth part, and 100
2 CONT messuages, 500a. land Cornish, 40a. meadow, 100a. wood, 100a. furze and heath and
2 CONT 100s. rent in Mayon, Boskenvyn, [Fentenleke], Penfenten[eowe, Rynsy,] Tregeusteke,
2 CONT Lanevett, Estals, Trevilly, Trewaseke Wartha, Trevaseke W[oles,] Trenals, Guyek,
2 CONT Greys, Gromeleighe, Pollech, Treyllyon, Bosioore, Baskett, Neuham, Parcoys,
2 CONT Lostwollythyell, Lanhunsyth, Tregentulyan, ‘Sent Colyns the ov[era’, Truruburgh,
2 CONT Trenans, Hendre in the parish of Seynt Kewa], Slygyowe, Buthen Gleeb, Tuneacker,
2 CONT Treloga, Tregelest, Pendoget, Tremetany, Hendre by Rynsy, Trewafos, Tregere, Trenowyth
2 CONT by Tregeere, Trevesewathen, Poltuske, Gwelmayow and Tregorreke.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORNWALL. Manor of Mayon, held of Thomas Leighton, knight, as of his manor of
2 CONT Corvoigth, by fealty and 5s. 10d. yearly rent and common suit to the court of the
2 CONT manor of Corvoigth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Boskenvyn, held of the prince, as of his manor of Helston in Kerrir, parcel
2 CONT of the duchy of Cornwall, by fealty and 4s. 6d. rent and common suit to the court of
2 CONT the manor aforesaid.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Fentenleke, held of John Arundell, knight, as of his manor of Conerton, by
2 CONT knight-service and 4s. rent, with common suit to the court of the said manor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Penfenteneowe, held of William Fortescue, Humphrey Monke and John Carmynowe,
2 CONT esquires, in right of their wives, [as of their manor of] Ethelyse, by fealty, 4s.
2 CONT rent, and common suit to the court of the manor aforesaid.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Rynsy, worth 53s. 4d., held, of William Trewynnard by fealty and 4s. 10d.
2 CONT rent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Tregeusteke, worth 4l., held of the manor of Blyston, late of Richard Nanfan,
2 CONT knight, by fealty and 20d. rent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Lanevett, worth 40s., held of the prior of Bodmyn, as of his manor of
2 CONT Ryalton, by fealty and 2s. 8d. rent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fourth part of the borough of Truru and a water-mill there, worth 13s. 4d., held of
2 CONT the prince in free burgage by fealty only.
2 CONT
2 CONT Land called ‘Guelemayoth,’ containing 40a. land English, worth 20s., held of the
2 CONT prince, as of his manor of Helston in Kerreerez, parcel of the duchy of Cornwall, by
2 CONT fealty and 3s. rent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan late the wife of Edmund Arundell, knight, held for life at the time of the death
2 CONT of Anne Crocker, and still holds, the under-mentioned manor and advowson.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORNWALL. Manor of Tremedert with the advowson of the church of Dewlo, worth
2 CONT 20l., held of the king, as of the manor of Latyan, formerly of the earl of Salisbury,
2 CONT by knight-service.
2 CONT
2 CONT The reversion of all the premises held for life by Anne late the wife of Remfrey
2 CONT Arundell and Joan late the wife of Edmund Arundell pertained to Anne Crocker
2 CONT aforesaid, and on her death descended to her heirs above-named.
2 CONT
2 CONT By a fine levied in the king’s court in the quinzaine of Midsummer, 1 Henry VII,
2 CONT William Houghton, knight, and Joan, his wife, granted the under-mentioned manors,
2 CONT messuages &c. to Robert Throgmerton, esquire, and Edward Bertlet, who by the same fine
2 CONT granted the premises back to the said William and Joan and the heirs of the body of
2 CONT Joan, with successive remainders to Thomas Nevyll, kinsman and heir of William Nevyll
2 CONT of Pykell, knight, in tail male, and to the right heirs of Guy de Blankmoustre, late
2 CONT rector of Lansalloys. Joan died 20 December, 13 Henry VII, and William remained seised
2 CONT of the premises in his demesne as of free tenement. After Joan’s death the reversion
2 CONT of the premises descended to Edmund Arundell, knight, kinsman and heir of the body of
2 CONT the said Joan, to wit, son of Remfrey, her son and heir by Remfrey Arundell, knight,
2 CONT her first husband. Edmund died 27 November, 19 Henry VII, without heir of his body,
2 CONT whereupon the said reversion descended to Anne aforesaid, wife of John Crokker, sister
2 CONT and heir of the said Edmund, as kinswoman and heir of the body of the said Joan, to
2 CONT wit, daughter of Remfrey her son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Crokker died 25 August last without heir of her body, whereupon the said
2 CONT reversion descended to Anne Danvers and John Whytyngton and Richard Bolles, esquires;
2 CONT Anne Danvers being the daughter of John Stradlyng son of Elizabeth the elder daughter
2 CONT of the aforesaid Joan by Remfrey Arundell, knight, her first husband, John Whytyngton
2 CONT being the son of Elizabeth the second daughter of the said Joan and Remfrey, and
2 CONT Richard Bolles being son of Isabel, daughter of the said Joan by John Nanfan, esquire,
2 CONT her second husband. At the time of death of Anne Crokker, Anne Danvers was aged 30
2 CONT years, John Whytyngton 44 years, and Richard Bolles 30 years and more. William
2 CONT Houghton aforesaid died the last day of February last.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORNWALL. Manors of Byenamye (worth 10l.), and Stratton (worth 20l.), held of
2 CONT the prince, as of his castle of Launceston, parcel of the duchy of Cornwall, by
2 CONT knight-service.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Sw[ancott], worth 40s., held as above.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Seynt Maryweke and Wekebourgh (Wike) and the advowson of Seynt Mary Weke,
2 CONT worth 10l., held as above.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Leskerd Colshull, worth 6l., held as above.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Seynt Clere Colshull, worth 6l., held of the heirs of Richard Derlyng by
2 CONT fealty only.
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 messuages, 2000a. land, 300a. meadow, 400a. pasture, 300a. wood and 100s. rent in
2 CONT Bynamye, Stratton, Swancote, Seynt Mary Weke, Seynt Clere Colshull, Leskerd Colshull
2 CONT and Tremyeth, held (except a messuage and 1a. land Cornish in Tremyeth) of the prince,
2 CONT as of the castle aforesaid, by knight-service; worth 20s. The said messuage and land
2 CONT in Tremyeth, worth 6s. 8d., are held of Thomas Cressy by fealty.
2 CONT
2 CONT C. Series II. Vol. 21. (10.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.british-history.ac.uk/inquis-post-mortem/series2-vol3/pp209-250
2 CONT
2 CONT 436. ANNE CROCKER, widow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Writ 30 October, inquisition 27 May, 23 Henry VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT By a fine levied in the quinzaine of St. John the Baptist, 1 Henry VII, between Robert
2 CONT Throgmerton, esquire, and Edward Berlet, querents, and William Houghton, knight, and
2 CONT Joan his wife, deforciants, the under-mentioned manors and lands were settled on the
2 CONT said William and Joan and the heirs of the body of Joan. Joan died 20 December, 13
2 CONT Henry VII, and William survived her and held himself in the premises by survivorship.
2 CONT After Joan’s death the reversion of the premises descended to Edmund Arundell, knight,
2 CONT as her kinsman and heir of her body, to wit, son of Remfrey her son and heir by
2 CONT Remfrey Arundell, knight, her first husband. Edmund died 27 November, 19 Henry VII,
2 CONT without heir of his body, whereupon the reversion descended to Anne wife of John
2 CONT Crokker, named in the writ, as kinswoman and heir of the body of the said Joan, to
2 CONT wit, daughter of the said Remfrey her son and heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne died 25 August last without heir of her body, whereupon the reversion descended
2 CONT to Anne wife of John Danvers, knight (daughter of John Stradlyng, son of Elizabeth,
2 CONT elder daughter of the said Joan by Remfrey Arundell), John Whytyngton, esquire (son of
2 CONT Elizabeth, second daughter of Joan by the said Remfrey), and Richard Bolles, esquire
2 CONT (son of Isabel, third daughter of the said Joan by John Nanffan, esquire, her second
2 CONT husband), as kinsfolk and heirs of the body of the said Joan. At the death of Anne
2 CONT Crocker, Anne Danvers was aged 30 years, John Whytyngton 44 years, and Richard Bolles
2 CONT 30 years. William Houghton aforesaid died the last day of February last.
2 CONT
2 CONT DEVON. Manor of Huysshe, with the advowson of the church of Huysshe, worth 5 marks,
2 CONT held of Margaret, countess of Richmond, as of her castle of Chepyng Torryngton, by
2 CONT service of a twentieth part of a knight’s fee.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manor of Stowford by Lyfton, with the advowson of the church of Stowford, worth 60s.,
2 CONT held of the same countess, as of her castle aforesaid, by service of a thirtieth part
2 CONT of a knight’s fee.
2 CONT
2 CONT 200a. land, 10a. meadow, 60a. furze and heath and 10a. moor in Bowreland, worth 20s.,
2 CONT held of Edward, earl of Devon, as of his castle of Okynhampton, in free socage, by
2 CONT service of a load of hay.
