1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Images
2 CONT https://amymcelroy.substack.com/p/st-marys-chilton-and-the-cranes
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.flickr.com/photos/52219527@N00/14382869595/
2 CONT The monument was made c10 years before Robert's death and placed in the chantry chapel he had built here. In his will he asked that "my body to holy sepultur that is to say in the tombe of alabaster standing in the chauncell of Ch
2 CONC ylton church"’. Anne in her will asked to be buried ‘"in the chapel annexed to Chilton Churche by the Grace of Robert Crane sumtyme my husband".
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Crane in his will of August 4, 1500, leaves "to my sister Appulton my Releqwikis aboute my nek," and appoints "my brother Thomas Appulton gentleman" (of Little Waldingfield) executor. (Thomas Appleton was the father of Thom
2 CONC as Appleton at Little Waldingfield
2 CONT
2 CONT The inquest on the estate of Robert Crane,in 1501, states that "he died without heir of his body begotten," (his only son George having died without issue in his lifetime)
