2 TITL Anders Ulff - descendents.pdf
1 NOTE
2 CONT Both Dyreskjøt and the Swedish genealogist Gabriel Angrep agree that 
2 CONT the Kjerulf family originally came from Holstein, and that the first 
2 CONT of this line to step into the "light of history" was Anders Ulff. We 
2 CONT have already told how he acquired the name Kjærulf. In Dyreskjøt's 
2 CONT book we read that he "owned the Aslundgaard "fogdegaard" (the farm 
2 CONT where the rural tax collector lived), the Biørum farm, and a lot of 
2 CONT property and farms in Kier township, as well as in Hvetbo and Hann 
2 CONT townships, and that he had a grey wolf in his coat of arms. He lived 
2 CONT at the time of King Erik of Pomerania (1430), King Christoffer of 
2 CONT Bavaria (1440) and King Christiern I (1450), a fact which is 
2 CONT documented in old letters."
2 CONT For Klitgaard it remains an open question whether Anders Ulff 
2 CONT belonged to the nobility or not. The other two genealogists, 
2 CONT Dyreskjøt and Gabriel Angrep believe that he was "introduced into 
2 CONT Danish nobility". The fact that he was a wealthy property owner and 
2 CONT had his own coat of arms would lead one to believe that he was a 
2 CONT nobleman, and the report that he was at the royal court and rendered 
2 CONT an "exceptional service" to the king further confirms that he was a 
2 CONT man of exalted station.
2 CONT It is said that he lived under three kings: Erik of Pomerania 
2 CONT (1387-1442), Kristoffer of Bavaria (1442), and Kristern I 
2 CONT (1450-1481). From this information one could surmise that he was born 
2 CONT about 1380 and died about 1450.
2 CONT Dyreskjøt writes: "I have never been able to find the name of his 
2 CONT wife, but do know the names of three of his sons."
2 CONT The line continued with these three sons, but we shall only deal with 
2 CONT one of them here.
1 NOTE Indført i adelskalenderen og tildelt navnet Kjærulff af Erik af Pommern for en ham bevist tjeneste. Førte en gående grå ulv i sit våben.
2 CONT Ejer af Aslund Gård i Ø. Hassing, Fogedgård i Vadum Sogn, Biørdum og meget gods i Kjær, Hvetbo og Hanherred.
1 NOTE Hans bondgård, Fogdegaard ligger utanför Vadum i Kjær distrikt i norra delen av Jylland bara 8 km nordväst om Aalborg. Den nuvarande gården byggdes 1735 efter det att Kjerulffs lämnade den 1684. En av byggnaderna på gården har for
2 CONC tfarande kvar orginal golv och väggar. En plaket sattes upp på väggen på Fogdegaard när gården besökten under Kiermeet90.
