1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * He was a National Judge in Skåne. http://roskildehistorie.dk/stamtavler/adel/Rosensparre/Rosensparre.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT * Roses, Skåne nobility, which can be traced back to Judge Johannes Nielsen of Skarhult (first mentioned 1353). The heyday of the family was in the 16th and 16th centuries, as it became part of the Danish nobility through marriage
2 CONC  and office. The genus thus obtained a seat in the council of two generations with Steen Rosensparre (1523-65) and his son, Oluf Rosensparre (1559-1624), with whom the genus died out on the male side.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johannes Nielsen Rosensparre'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Af Skarholt (Froste H.), beseglede 1353 et Vidne af Skaane Landsthing, var 1355 Landsdommer i Skaane. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Danmarks Adels Aarbog, Thiset, Hiort-Lorenzen, Bobé, Teisen., (Dansk Adelsforening), [1884 - 2011]., DAA 1899:371.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT '''Johannes Nielsen Rosensparre'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fødsel:	før 1330 Skarhult, Skåne, Sverige (Sweden) 
2 CONT * Dødsfald:	efter 1370 Skarholt Slott, Skarhult, Skåne, Sverige (Sweden) 
2 CONT * Occupation:	Landsdommer i Skaane. 1355. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Søn af Niels Rosensparre 
2 CONT * Gift med NN 
2 CONT * Far til Jep Jensen Rosensparre 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
