1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Jon Arnesson Giske=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Parents: Arne Arnesson & Gjertrud Erlingsdatter 
2 CONT * Birth: circa 1033 in Giske, Møre og Romsdal, Norway
2 CONT * Death:	1097 (60-68) in Bjarkøy, Harstad, Troms, Norway
2 CONT * Sigurd's son Asbjørn Selsbane was killed by the king's men, but Tore Hund's son, Sigurd Toresson from Bjarkøy , had no son, but a daughter,Ragnhild Sigurdsdatter , who was married to Giskeætten by Jon Arnesson from Giske , son o
2 CONC f Arne Arnesson . Jon is descended from Erling Skjalgsson at Sola and Astrid Tryggvesdatter , sister of King Olav Tryggvason . Ragnhild and Jon had their son Vidkun Jonsson from Bjarkøy who participated in King Magnus Berrføtt's a
2 CONC rmy in Ireland. Sigurd Jorsalfares son Magnus was raised at Vidkun in Bjarkøy. - https://no.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bjark%C3%B8y%C3%A6tten
2 CONT * Jon is mentioned in connection with Steigar-Tor's rebellion, supposedly in 1095. He and his son Vidkun was on Bjarkøy when Tore and several of the rebels came there by ship.  They had to flee, while Tor's people stole everything
2 CONC  and burned the farm and a good long ship belonging to Bidkun. Both traveled south and met Magnus Barfot, who went north with them and met Tore in the Harem fjord, around Torget and Brønnøy. After a brief fight, Tore was caught an
2 CONC d hanged.
2 CONT * Nordic Family Book from 1876 says about Jon: 2) The Bjarkö family. Arne Arnesson was like that the brothers Torberg a faithful supporter of Olof it Saints, even though he was married to a daughter to Erling Skjalgsson. When Olof
2 CONC  returned to Norway, A. joined him and became severely wounded in the battle of Stiklastad. His son Jon married one daughter of Tore Hund and heritage thereby pedigree Bjarkö. Jon's son was the one from Magnus Barfots last Ireland
2 CONC  train (1103) known Vidkunn Jonsson, whose son Erling under the peoples the war belonged to Magnus Erlingsson's party. Her son Vidkunn Erlingsson stayed at the age of 18 (1183) killed by Sverre's supporters. With him educated the 
2 CONC family, and Bjarkö went through his sister Ragnas marriage to the lawyer in Hålogaland Bjarne Mardsson. From them descended "it younger Bjarkö family, who later also inherited Giske.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: ''' Ranveig / Ragnhild Sigurdsdotter Hund, av Bjarkøy,''' daughter of Sigurd Toresson Hund, of Bjarkøy and Audur Unn Snorresdotter 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Vidkunn Jonsson,''' born about 1066, died after 1138. Was the foster father of Magnus Blinde.
2 CONT *''' Erling Jonsson, av Bjarkøy;''' birth: circa 1068 in Bjarkøy, Harstad, Troms, Norway
2 CONT *''' Gjertrud Jonsdatter Giske Bjarkøy;''' birth: circa 1070 in Bjarkøy, Troms, Norway
2 CONT * '''Sigurd Hund;''' Lyst Peaceless by King Magnus Barfot. Without known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon Arnesson Giske was born ca in Bjarkøy, Troms, Norway, died in 1097 in Bjarkøy, Troms, Norway at the age of about 64, and was buried in Bjarkøy, Norway. General notes: The Nordic Family Book from 1876 says about Jon: 2) The Bja
2 CONC rkö family. Arne Arnesson, like the brothers Torberg, was a faithful supporter of Olof the saint, even though he was married to a daughter of Erling Skjalgsson. When Olof returned to Norway, A. joined him and became severely injur
2 CONC ed in the battle at Stiklastad. His son Jon married a daughter of Tore Hund and inherited her pedigree Bjarkö. Jon's son was Vidkunn Jonsson, known from Magnus Barfot's last Irish train (1103), whose son Erling belonged to Magnus 
2 CONC Erlingsson's party during the war between her. Vidkunn Erlingsson's son, at the age of 18 (1183), was killed by Sverre's supporters. With him the family educated, and Bjarkö went through his sister Ragna's marriage to the lawyer i
2 CONC n Hålogaland Bjarne Mardsson. From them, "the younger Bjarkö family", which later also inherited Giske Jon Arneson, was descended from Arnmødlingicts at Giske in Sundmøre. He got Bjarkøygodset with his wife when he married. When S
2 CONC teiga-Tore rebelled mother King Magnus Berrføtt in 1094 Jon had  his farm burnt down, and he had to flee. But had Steiga-Tore hanged Jon Arnesson Parents Arne Arnesson Gjertrud Erlingsdatter Marriages and children Married to Ranve
2 CONC ig Sigurddatter, with Vidkunn Jonsson Bjarkøy Sigurd Hund Jonsson Sources: - person: Bjarkøy village book 1947, bd 1, page 131 1883, by Peder Fylling - family: Bjarkøy village book 1947, bd 1, page 131 Ranveig Sigurdsdatter Parent
2 CONC s Sigurd Toresson at Bjarkøy Aud Snorresdatter Marriages and children Married to Jon Arnesson, with Vidkunn Jonsson Bjarkøy Sigurd Hund Jonsson Sources: - person: Bjarkøy village book 1947, bd 1, page 131 Giskeæten at Søndmør, s 2
2 CONC , Ålesund 1883, by Peder Fylling Tønsber Blad 13 /, Over mountain and valley, by Finn Wang - family: Bjarkøy village book 1947, bd 1, page Jon Arnesson Parents Arne Arnesson Gjertrud Erlingsdatter Marriages and children Married to
2 CONC  Ranveig Sigurdsdatter, with 213
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://runeberg.org/nfaa/1107.html Project Runeberg]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) The Bjarkö family.  Like the Torberg brothers, Arne Arnesson was a faithful follower of Olof the Holy, despite the fact that he was also married to a daughter of Erling Skjalgsson.  When Olof returned to Norway, A. joined him a
2 CONC nd was severely wounded in the battle of Stiklastad. '''His son Jon married a daughter of Tore Hund and thereby inherited his ancestral estate Bjarkö. Jon's son was the well-known Vidkunn Jonsson from Magnus Barfot's last Irish tr
2 CONC ain (1103), whose son Erling during the mutual the wars belonged to Magnus Erlingsson's party.''' His son Vidkunn Erlingsson was killed at the age of 18 (1183) by Sverre's followers. With him the family died out and Bjarkö went th
2 CONC rough to his sister Ragnar's marriage to the lawyer in Hålogaland Bjarne Mardsson . From them descended the " 
2 CONT younger Bjarkö family", who later also inherited Giske. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigurd_Toresson_fra_Bjark%C3%B8y Sigurd Toresson, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT With Aud, Sigurd had his daughter Ragnhild Sigurdsdatter who was strategically married to Jon Arnesson from Giske, son of Arne Arnesson, and he descended from Erling Skjalgsson at Sola and Astrid Tryggvesdatter, sister of Olav Try
2 CONC ggvason. Ragnhild and Jon had their son Vidkun Jonsson from Bjarkøy, who is mentioned several times in the king's sagas.  Snorre Sturlasson also mentions that Ragnhild and Jon had children Sigurd Hund, Erling Jonsson and Jartrud J
2 CONC onsdatter.
2 CONT
