1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ='''Gregorius Dagsson'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT Lendmann Gregorius Jonson of Blind Heims Ætta in Sunnmøre
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Dag Eilivsson Bratsberg and Ragnhild Skoftedotter 
2 CONT * Gregorius Dagsson, D. 1161. He was an Ampman, owned and lived after his father in the great Bratsberg farm in Gjerpen. This farm received both the backrest and the Amt Bratsberg name after (Telemark County). Gregorius was the he
2 CONC ad of the great-man party who was under the contention between the sons of Harald Gille (d. 1136) and supported the best and least self-righteous of them, King Inge Krokrygg (d. 1161). During the fight, Bratsberg Gård was burned b
2 CONC y the brother of the King Eystein Haraldsson (d. 1157). Gregorius fell into battle with Eystein's son Håkon Herdebreid (d. 1162) near Kongshelle.
2 CONT * He was a lover, owned and lived after his father on the large farm Bratsberg in Gjerpen. This farm got both the lace and the county Bratsberg named after (Telemark county). Gregory was the leader of the Grand Duchy as under the 
2 CONC struggles between the sons of Harald Gille (d.1136) and supported the best and least self-righteous of them, King Inge Krokrygg (d.1161). During the fight, Bratsberg farm was burned by Inge's brother, King Eystein Haraldsson (d.11
2 CONC 57). Gregory fell in battle with Eystein's son Håkon Herdebreid (d.1162) near Kongshelle.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://nbl.snl.no/Gregorius_Dagsson Gregorius Dagsson BY: Narve Bjørgo (University of Bergen)]
2 CONT
2 CONT THIS ARTICLE WAS PRINTED IN THE NORWEGIAN BIOGRAPHICAL LEXICON, WRITTEN BY: Narve Bjørgo (University of Bergen)
2 CONT
2 CONT Newer articles can be found in the large Norwegian encyclopedia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lendmann. Parents: Lend The man day Eilivsson (sjto NBL1, Bd. 3) and Ragnhild Skoftesdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fact: DEAD January 7, 1161
2 CONT * PLACE OF DEATH Ranrike (no KUNGÄLV, Sweden), buried in Gimsøy, a convent at Skien
2 CONT * LIFETIME COMMENT Birth year and birthplace are unhereous
2 CONT * Birth year and birthplace are unhereous
2 CONT * Gregorius Dagsson was at the time in 1150, the dominant military and political tenant in the Krinsen broadcasting Inge Krokrygg (Inge 1 Haraldsson). A country-like aristocratic gathering of Inge seems to have also his superior's
2 CONC  political goals.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gregorius had close family and moon bands to the King's Ætta and to the multiple of the most powerful great man's genera in the country. Mora Ragnhild Skoftesdotter was the father of Giskeætta, and his maternal grandfather, and Mu
2 CONC ndsson, was the younger child of King Olav Haraldsson Kyrre. He was the foster-brother of King Inge Krokrygg, a man-in-law. Through the poison moon to the syrups of Borghild Dagdotter and Sigrid Dagdotter, Gregorius stood in the b
2 CONC rother-in-law of the Orcman's ætes at Austrått in Sør-Trøndelag and Vetteland in Ranrike. The Reformation and friendship relationships of this battle created the foundations of a party prega political interest fellowship between p
2 CONC owerful Losians in the Borgarkrigstida, with Gregorius Dagsson as the central driver and the tenant in the 1150 year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Heimskringla delving Gregorius as "the chairman of the national force with King Inge", after the connection from 1154. First of all, we meet him as a military strategist and active Krigar, and he was the hauler behind Drapa on Kin
2 CONC g Inge's Samkongebrør Sigurd Haraldsson Munn (1155) and Øystein Haraldsson (1157). In this systematic liquidation, the road to Inge Krokrygg was supposed to be the same as the family of the Mektigaste and the church. The special H
2 CONC eimskringla gave a detailed correlation to Gregory of the planar and Overtala's time-to-the-standard to join this line, after a quarter of the competition's concoation. His key role is also emphasized by the attack King Øystein st
2 CONC raightened against the genealogies of Gregorius – Bratsberg in Gjerpen – the Hausten the same year in which King Sigurd was killed in Bergen.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the assassination of King Øystein 1157, Gregorius had regularly halted in the southern frontier area with the centre of Konghelle. The reason is Tydeleg: Among the "River grim" in this part of the Reich, it was for new oppos
2 CONC ition groups to win support against King Inge, but Gregorius's military presence was to prevent. The parishionals depict the multiple struggles of the Treaty of Konghelle, and from one of the Stridane, there have been preserved a 
2 CONC pair of skull-sculpts of Einar skulasons Elfarvisur (River Show), a poem in which Gregorius was a mayor.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Erling Skakke, the tenant of the mighty Støle Ætta at Etne in Sunnhordland, was cheerfull in the midst of the 1150-year, and was named Gregorius Dagsson a competitor as a clay figure in the Krinsen broadcasting Inge. In dist
2 CONC inctive steps, the sagas, Erling and Gregorius, are the founding of various Personlegdomar, who gladly gave the King various counsel in military tactical issues. From 1159, it gradually built up a very tense rise between the two a
2 CONC nd the houses of Deira, a great concern for King Inge. Truleg was the death of Gregorius Dagsson on the ice for Konghelle January 1161, contrary to the king Håkon Sigurdsson Herdebreid, who would prevent a confrontation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Heimskringla Fortel to King Inge's death message about the assassination of Gregorius, he was a child of the loss of his "best friend," he who "most has befriended the land in my hands". The men of Gregorius end loyally up about E
2 CONC rling Skakkes ' tenant after the Deira River chief was gone. It is in itself a strong testimony of organizational power in the Viking-western loam party.
2 CONT
2 CONT The distinctive Heimskringla is the 1150-year from the Inge party's Synsstad, Noko who in itself had to give Breistein and positive mention of Gregorius Dagsson. But there is no doubt that he had a significant dimension as a milit
2 CONC ary strategist. He exhibited with the 90 Huskarar and two longships, and such krigarfølgje formed the core of the time military apparatus. The host stressed that Gregorius was treating his men more than other lendmen, and they wer
2 CONC e all equipped with a helmet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gregorius is being parted as a Praktglad man, who wore a gold helmet when he was Reid to Tings. By nature, he could be angry and abrupt, but first and foremost, the action-oriented, and with great Tru on the power of battle as a c
2 CONC ombat strategy. Among the standards, this has been given the reputation of the war hawk. One side of his character was expressed in an episode in the Stur Lunga saga, in which he was the protector of a refugee couple from Iceland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Saga tradition portrututaneous Gregorius as a man of great wealth. The core of his freight collection was the Ætte garden Bratsberg in Gjerpen (no Skien), Telemark. After the murder, his body was brought home and buried in Gim
2 CONC søy Monastery, which was founded by the father of Gregorius, and his systera, Baugeid Dagdotter, was the abbot.
2 CONT
