1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Orm Sveinsson Kyrpinga-Orm=
2 CONT
2 CONT * The family descended from Erlend av Gerde (Gjerde in Etne), who was one of the farmers' leaders in the Battle of Stiklestad in 1030. Erlend's grandson was the employed lieutenant Orm Sveinsson (Kyrpinga-Orm). Orm's son Erling Sk
2 CONC akke married Sigurd Jorsalfare's daughter Kristin, and he was the father of King Magnus Erlingsson . Both Kyrpinga-Orm and Erling Skakke lived in Stødle.
2 CONT * Orm "Kyrpinge-Orm" as he was named after the farm Kyrping in Etne in Sunnhordland, was the grandson of the lieutenant Erlend from Gjerde
2 CONT * Orm, was the foster father of the king's son Magnus Haraldsson 
2 CONT * Orm Svenson in Korpinge, called Korpinge-Orm; Länes-Höfdinge in Norway. - Married to Drottning Ragnild; daughter of a rich Länes-Höfdinge in Wiken (Bohus län) Sverker Stjernardsson and widow of King Magnus Håkansson in Norway. 
2 CONT * [http://runeberg.org/anrep/3/0375.html '''von Nackreij - Skytte, Volume 3, page 371''']
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWAY.htm#ErlingOrmsenMKristinSigurdsdatter Project MedLands, NORWAY KINGS]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SVEN Svensson, son of ERLING of Gerd & his wife''' ---.  Snorre names "Svein Svenson…a son of Erling of Gerd"[504].  '''married RAGNA Ormsdatter, daughter of ORM Eilifsson & his wife Sigrid Finnsdotter.'''  Snorre names "Ragna,
2 CONC  a daughter of Earl Orm Eilifson and Sigrid, a daughter of Earl Fin Arnason" as mother of "Otto"[505]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sven & his wife had RAGNA one child:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''ORM Svensson "Krypinge-Orm" (-[1140]).'''  Snorre names "Kyrpingaorm…a son of Svein Svenson"[506].  '''married firstly RAGNHILD Skulesdatter,''' daughter of SKULI Tostesson "Kongsfostre".  '''married secondly RAGNH
2 CONC ILD Svenkesdatter, daughter of SVENKE Steinarsson & his wife''' ---.  Snorre names "Ragnhild, a daughter of Sveinke Steinarson" as the wife of "Kyrpingaorm"[507].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ORM Svensson "Krypinge-Orm" & his first wife RAGNHILD Skulesdatter, had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* i)          '''OGMUND Dreng''' (-1155).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   Guardian of Inge I King of Norway.
2 CONT >>>>>* ii)         '''ASA'''  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   '''married NIKOLAS, son of ?.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ORM Svensson "Krypinge-Orm" & his second wife RAGNHILD Svenkesdatter had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* iii)        '''ERLING Ormson "Skakke/the Sharp" of Studla in South Hordaland''' (-killed in battle near Nidaros [Trondheim] 19 Jun 1179, bur Trondheim Cathedral).  Snorre names Erling as the son of "Kyrpingaorm and Ragnhild
2 CONC , a daughter of Sveinke Steinarson", when recording that he possessed a farm at Studla in South Hordaland and journeyed to Palestine with Kali-Ragnvald Jarl of Orkney[508].  Regent of Norway in 1162 for his son King Magnus V.  Jar
2 CONC l in Norway 1170.  '''The Saga of King Sverre records that "Earl Erling" was killed in battle near Nidaros fighting King Sverre, and was buried in Trondheim church[509]. ''' The precise date of his death is recorded in an Icelandi
2 CONC c Obituarium[510].  '''married  (1155) KRISTIN Sigurdsdatter, daughter of SIGURD King of Norway & his second wife Malmfred Mstislavna of Kiev ([1125]-1178).'''  Snorre names "Christina, a daughter of King Sigurd the Crusader and Q
2 CONC ueen Malmfrid" as the wife of Erling[511].  This is confirmed by the Saga of King Sverre records the marriage of "Ragnhild daughter of Earl Erling and Kristin Kings-daughter" and "Halkel son of Jon Hallkelsson"[512].  '''Mistress 
2 CONC (1): ---.  The name of Erling's mistress is not known.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Erling & his wife KRISTIN Sigurdsdatter had two children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>* (a)       '''MAGNUS Erlingsson''' (1156-killed in battle near Fimreite on Sognefjord 15 Jun 1184, bur Bergen, Christ's Church).  Snorre names Magnus Erlingson as son of "Kristin…daughter of King Sigurd the Crusader" when
2 CONC  recording that he "was nearest by propinquity of descent to the crown of Norway", and elected king of the whole country when aged five[513].  '''He succeeded in 1161 as MAGNUS King of Norway.'''  Snorre Sturlsons's Heimskringla e
2 CONC nds with King Magnus's victory against King Eystein [in 1177][514].  The Saga of King Sverre records that King Sverre defeated King Magnus at Iluvelli [27 May 1180], after which Magnus "sailed…to Denmark to his kinsman Valdamar"[5
2 CONC 15].  The Saga of King Sverre records that King Magnus was killed in battle at "Norafiord" by King Sverre and was buried at Christ's Church, Bergen[516].  The Icelandic Annals record that "Magni regis, Erlingi filii" was killed "a
2 CONC  Sverrero" in 1184[517].  '''married as her second husband, ELDRID Bjørnsdatter, widow of TORE Skinnfeld,  daughter of BJØRN Byrdasvein & his wife Rangrid Guttormsdatter.  Mistress (1): GYRID Aslaksdatter, daughter of ASLAK & his 
2 CONC wife.'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''King Magnus & his wife ELDRID Bjørnsdatter, had two children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* (1)       '''INGEBJÖRG Magnusdatter''' (-on crusade with her husband 1213).  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1213 of "Petrus Steyperus, uxorque eius Ingeburga, filia regis Magni Erlingii filii"[518].  '''marri
2 CONC ed  (before 1204) PETER Stöype [stormand of the Birkebene], possibly son of a sister of Sverre King of Sweden (-on crusade with his wife 1213).'''
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* (2)       '''MARGRET Magnusdatter.  married firstly (before 1206) FILIPPUS of Vegin [stormand of the Bagler] (-1207).  married secondly (before 1208) REIDAR Sendemand [stormand of the Bagler] (-Constantinople 1214).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''King Magnus had one illegitimate child by Mistress (1):''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* (3)        '''SIGURD Magnusson''' (-killed in battle Florevåg near Bergen 3 Apr 1194, bur Bergen Church of St Mary).  The Saga of King Sverre names "a boy named Sigurd a son of King Magnus Erlingson" as one of the cons
2 CONC pirators with "Halkel son of Jon Hallkelsson"[519].  King of the Øyskjegger in Norway 1192.  The Saga of King Sverre records that "Sigurd Kingsson" was killed in battle "in the water at Floruvoe" and was buried in "Marinkirk yard"
2 CONC [520]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''King Magnus had four possible illegitimate children by unknown mistresses:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* (4)       ''' [VIKAR] Magnusson''' (-killed in battle near Bridstein 1190).  King of the Varbelger in Norway 1189.  He claimed the throne.]
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* (5)       '''INGE [Magnusson]''' (-murdered Helgøya, Mjøsa 1202).  The Saga of King Sverre records that "the Bagals…at Borg" chose "King Magnus's son Ingi" as their king and that the whole of the Vik and the Uplands su
2 CONC bmitted to him[521].  King of the Bagals in Norway 1196. 
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* (6)        '''[ERLING "Steinvegg/Stonewall" (-Tønsberg 1207, bur Tønsberg, Olavskyrka).'''  King of the Bagler in Norway 1204.  The Icelandic Annals record that "Erlingus Steinveggus" was raised to "regiam dignitatem" 
2 CONC in 1204[522].]  '''m ?.  The name of Erling's wife is not known.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ERLING "Steinvegg/Stonewall" & his wife had two children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>>>* a.          '''MAGNUS Erlingsson''' (1199-young).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>>>* b.          '''SIGURD Erlingsson "Ribbung''' (1203-Oslo 1226).  King of the Ribbunger in Norway: the Icelandic Annals record that "Sigurdus Erlingi filius" became "rex Ribbungorum" in 1221[523].'''  The Icelandic Ann
2 CONC als record the death in 1226 of "Sigurdus…rex Ribbungorum" and the succession of "domicellus Canutus Haquini filius" as leader of "Ribbungis" and his elevation to "regiam dignitatem"[524]. 
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>*(7)       ''' [BENE "Skinnkniv" (-murdered 1222).'''  Priest.  Stormann of the Slittunger in Norway 1218.  The Icelandic Annals record that "Benonis ducis Slittungorum" was killed in 1222[525].]
2 CONT >>>>>>>>* (b)       '''RAGNHILD Erlingsdatter.'''  Snorre names Ragnhild as "a daughter of princess Kristin and Earl Erling who was married to Jon Thorbergson of Randaberg", recording that she "went away from the country with a ma
2 CONC n called Grim Rusle…to Constantinople where they were for a time and had some children"[526].  The Saga of King Sverre records the marriage of "Ragnhild daughter of Earl Erling and Kristin Kings-daughter" and "Halkel son of Jon Ha
2 CONC llkelsson"[527].  '''married firstly JON Thorbergsson from Randaberg''' (-killed in battle near Nidaros [Trondheim] 18 or 19 Jun 1179).  '''married secondly HALLKEL Jonsson from Blindheim Jarl in Norway, son of JON Hallkelsson & h
2 CONC is wife Margrete of Norway [daughter of King Harald Gille] (-killed in battle Florevåg near Bergen 3 Apr 1194).''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Erling had one illegitimate child by Mistress (1):''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>>>* (c)        '''SIGURD'''   The Saga of King Sverre names "an illegitimate son of Earl Erling named Sigurd a foster-son of King Sverri" as one of the conspirators with "Halkel son of Jon Hallkelsson"[528]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Soga_um_Inge  Heimskringla Soga (kap 17)]
2 CONT
2 CONT 17. Kyrpinga-Orm and Ragnhild, his daughter Sveinke Steinarsson, had a son named Erling. His father's KyrpingaOrm was named Svein, and he was the son of Svein Erlendsson from Gjerde [59]. His mother Orm was Ragna, who was the daug
2 CONC hter of Earl Orm Eilivsson [60] and Sigrid [61], who was the daughter of Earl Finn Arneson. Earl Orm Eilivsson's mother was Ragnhild, daughter of Earl Haakon the mighty. Erling was a wise man and a good friend of King Inge, and wi
2 CONC th his consent Erling Kristin, daughter of King Sigurd Jorsalafar and Queen Malmfrid. Erling had a farm on Studla [62] on Sunnhordaland. Erling went [1150] out of the country, and with him accompanied Eindride Unge and even more l
2 CONC ieutenants, and had a beautiful here. They set out on a Jorsala voyage and went west across the sea to the Orkney Islands. From there Earl Rognvald was with them, whom they called Kale, and Bishop Vilhjalm, and they had a total of
2 CONC  15 longships, when they sailed from the Orkney Islands, and so they sailed to the Sudrøyans and from there [1151] west to Valland and then the same road as King Sigurd Jorsalafar had gone out to Norvasund, and ravaged far and wid
2 CONC e in the heathen Spain. Immediately after they had sailed through sound, Eindride Unge parted, and those who followed him, with 6 ships from them, and then they left for themselves. Earl Rognvald and Erling Skakke fell into the se
2 CONC a on a dromund [63] and docked with 9 ships and fought with him. At last the carpenters laid their ranks under the dromund, and then the heathens threw down on them both weapons and stones and pots full of boiling dog and oil. Erl
2 CONC ing lay closest to them with his ship, so weapons to the heathens came outside his ship. Then Erling and his men cut holes in the dromund, some in the waterway and some up on the ship's deck, so they slipped in there. This is what
2 CONC  Torbjørn Skakke-skald told in Erlingsdraapa. The man who first went up on the dromund, was called Audun Raude and was his ancestor Erling. They took the dream and killed a lot of people and got a lot of booty and won a glorious s
2 CONC aying. On this voyage Earl Rognvald and Erling Skakke came to Jorsalaland and out to Jordan-aai. There they turned and went first to Miklegard, and there they left the ship and went home by land, and everything went well [1153], u
2 CONC ntil they came to Norway, and they went big word of this journey. Erling now went on to be a much greater man than before, both by this skill and by his marriage goal; he was attaat a wise man, rich and great-granddaughter and wor
2 CONC d-hitter, and he kept himself in all things most friends with King Inge of the three brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Stødle family, Norwegian nobility from the Middle Ages, named after the farm Stødle (now Støle) in Etne, Sunnhordland. The family descended from Erlend av Gerde (Gjerde in Etne), who was one of the farmers' leaders in the batt
2 CONC le of Stiklestad 1030. Erlend's grandson's son was the employed lieutenant Orm Sveinsson (Kyrpinga-Orm). Orm's son Erling (Skakke) married Sigurd Jorsalfare's daughter Kristine, and was the father of King Magnus Erlingsson. Both K
2 CONC yrpinga-Orm and Erling Skakke lived in Stødle.
2 CONT
